arm64: dts: qcom: add Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 family common dtsi

Add factored sm8550-samsung-gts9-common.dtsi for Tab S9 family-shared
content (SoC-plumbing + minimum PMIC includes matching sm8550-samsung-q5q
subset at v7.0.6 + reserved-memory baseline + console + BT serdev parent
UART). Per DEC-119 + DEC-196 + RFT-116 (~800-1000 LoC target scope
anchored against mainline precedents msm8916-samsung-a2015 + sony-nagara
+ q5q + lemans-ride).

For ubuntu-tab milestone-1, this is a skeleton; full body iterative
across milestone-1 follow-on + milestone-2 first-boot driver-binding
refinements. Per-SKU leaf DTS files (sm8550-samsung-x710.dts X710 base
+ sm8550-samsung-x810.dts X810 mid + sm8550-samsung-x910.dts X910 Ultra)
#include this file.

PMIC includes at skeleton subset: pm8550 + pm8550vs + pmk8550 (matches
sm8550-samsung-q5q.dts; minimum sufficient for clean dtc compile).
Additional PMICs (pm8550b, pm8550ve, pm8010) deferred to M2+ when
regulator nodes are authored that need them. pmr735d.dtsi not in v7.0.6
mainline (verified empirically); when needed, either wait for upstream
via konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com funnel or author a local patch in
the ubuntu-tab-x910 series.

Bootstrap source: Samsung downstream gts9uwifi_eur_open_w00_r03.dts SHA
74a08fac (SoC-plumbing + regulators + PCIe-enablement layer; mainline-
cleaned).

Signed-off-by: ubuntu-tab project <omarfityan@outlook.com>

Index: ubuntu-tab-x910/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-samsung-gts9-common.dtsi
===================================================================
--- /dev/null
+++ ubuntu-tab-x910/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-samsung-gts9-common.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 family common DTSI
+ * Shared SoC-plumbing + family-common bindings for:
+ *   - SM-X710 (Tab S9 base 11" Wi-Fi; codename gts9wifi)
+ *   - SM-X810 (Tab S9+ mid; codename gts9plus)
+ *   - SM-X910 (Tab S9 Ultra Wi-Fi; codename gts9uwifi — this project's target)
+ *
+ * Per:
+ * - ADR-0020 (R14) D1 + D2 factor-out common.dtsi architecture
+ * - DEC-119 (sess-27) single per-board DTS + factor common.dtsi
+ * - DEC-196 (sess-46) SKU-keyed leaf filenames + codename in compatible
+ * - RFT-116 (sess-40) common.dtsi LoC ~800-1000 anchored against mainline
+ *   precedents (msm8916-samsung-a2015 + sony-nagara + q5q + lemans-ride)
+ *
+ * Bootstrap source: Samsung downstream gts9uwifi_eur_open_w00_r03.dts
+ * SHA 74a08fac (SoC-plumbing + regulators + PCIe-enablement layer; q5q
+ * mainline NOT useful Wi-Fi/BT precedent per RFT-164; useful at
+ * SoC-plumbing layer only).
+ */
+
+#include "sm8550.dtsi"
+#include "pm8550.dtsi"
+#include "pm8550vs.dtsi"
+#include "pmk8550.dtsi"
+/*
+ * Skeleton PMIC subset matches sm8550-samsung-q5q.dts (Z-Fold5) at v7.0.6
+ * mainline — minimum set sufficient to compile without un-instantiated
+ * regulator references.
+ *
+ * Iterative additions at M2+/M3+ as regulator nodes get authored:
+ *   - pm8550b.dtsi (USB-PD-class PMIC)
+ *   - pm8550ve.dtsi (note: requires `#define PMK8550VE_SID <N>` before
+ *     #include in the LEAF .dts per qcom convention; e.g. sm8550-qrd.dts
+ *     uses SID 5; the includer parameterizes the SID at use time)
+ *   - pm8010.dtsi (peripheral PMIC)
+ *
+ * pmr735d.dtsi NOT IN v7.0.6 mainline (verified empirically at sess-67
+ * M1.5.3). Samsung uses pmr735d for Snapdragon power-regulator complex.
+ * Iterative authoring at M2+: either (a) wait for upstream pmr735d.dtsi
+ * via konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com funnel + linux-arm-msm list, or
+ * (b) author a local pmr735d.dtsi patch in the ubuntu-tab-x910 series
+ * if first-boot regulator dependencies surface as blockers.
+ */
+
+/ {
+	#address-cells = <2>;
+	#size-cells = <2>;
+
+	aliases {
+		serial0 = &uart7;     /* console UART; pinctrl placeholder */
+		serial1 = &uart14;    /* BT serdev parent per DEC-177 / RFT-119 */
+	};
+
+	chosen {
+		stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8";
+	};
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/*
+		 * Reserved-memory regions are derived from Samsung downstream
+		 * and mainline-cleaned. Full region layout extracted from
+		 * gts9uwifi_eur_open_w00_r03.dts SHA 74a08fac at iterative
+		 * authoring; for milestone-1 skeleton, leave empty so dtc
+		 * compiles.
+		 *
+		 * RFT-159 (sess-13 round-2): SoC dtsi default reserved-memory
+		 * map wrong; q5q deletes 5 reserved-memory regions. Apply same
+		 * approach: subtract from sm8550.dtsi defaults + add Tab S9
+		 * family-specific regions.
+		 */
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * Family-common peripheral enables.
+ *
+ * For milestone-1 skeleton, only the load-bearing UART (console + BT serdev
+ * parent) bindings are present. Full bindings (Wi-Fi/BT PCIe per R23 D1 + D2
+ * + D4, Wacom EMR per RFT-118 family-wide, touchscreen common parent bus per
+ * R20 D3, sensor bus parents per R17 D1, etc.) land at iterative authoring
+ * sess-67+ as needed for each driver to bind.
+ */
+
+&uart7 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&uart14 {
+	status = "okay";
+	/* BT serdev child node lives in leaf x910.dts per R23 ADR-0016 D2 */
+};
